Z||000000||ArchMagi||08-02-2001||09:16 PM||||Just wondering who had it? and if any pics of the shifter installed in a car are floating around.<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>87 Base Coupe with 168,000KM<BR>4cyl, 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000001||BENGAL4||08-02-2001||10:21 PM||||I just installed one 2 days ago, and i love it. Rodney's great to do business with too. Installation is easy. Remove an e clip and a cotter pin and your halfway home. Took about 15 minutes. get one you will love it.<P><BR>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 Series II S/C||||reg||10
Z||000002||Cheever2||08-02-2001||10:34 PM||||Here's some more opinions... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005749.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005749.html</A> <P>I have the dogleg shortened shifter which I still thank V8FieroGT for selling to me, but someday I will buy Rodney's straight one.  Is it true his is even <I>lengthened - <B>below the fulcrum point -</B></I> to maximize (or minimize, depending how you look at it) the action even more?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-02-2001||10:48 PM||||I've had mine for about 6 months.  I love it.  Third gear is a little bit of a stretch if you have short arms, but it works well with AusFieros sub box.  As a matter of fact, the two should be sold together.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||08-02-2001||11:48 PM||||I love it!  Have had it for a while now.  The action feels very crisp and almost a gated like feel.  The boot that comes with it looks great too.  I shortened mine 1/2", and I might do even more.<P>It really isnt that much harder to operate, your arms should already be strong from the lack of power steering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||08-03-2001||09:11 AM||||I've got Rodney's Comp Short Shifter.  It was a piece of cake to install, and seems to be a very well made unit.  I agree with everyone's comments above.  5th gear is a long way away, but it's not bad once you get used to it.  I've been playing with different shift knobs on it.  The picture below has an old Camaro knob, which I found to be too "short" for the 5th gear throw.  I've got a stock plastic Fiero knob on it now, and that seems to make it better.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/v8_interior_sm.jpg"> <P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>||||reg||14
